# libvita2d (core subset), vendored

Upstream: https://github.com/xerpi/libvita2d, commit
`a8f15ab09d5233f0a4e4ad0e8f6ade0da888cbed` (2021-11-26).  MIT licence, see
`LICENSE`.  Built by `gpsp/vita/ui.mk` into the Vita frontend; used only by
`gpsp/vita/vback_vita2d.c`.

The VitaSDK on the build machine has no vita2d package (and no libpng,
libjpeg or freetype to build the whole library against), so only the files
the video layer needs are here:

| here | upstream | |
|---|---|---|
| `source/vita2d.c` | `libvita2d/source/vita2d.c` | GXM set-up, scenes, clipping, the vertex pool |
| `source/vita2d_draw.c` | same | coloured primitives |
| `source/vita2d_texture.c` | same | textures, render targets, textured primitives |
| `source/utils.c` | same | GPU memory, matrices |
| `include/*.h` | `libvita2d/include/` | |
| `shader/*_gxp.o` | `libvita2d/shader/compiled/` | the seven precompiled shader programs (ARM ELF objects holding the `.gxp` binaries); `shader/*.cg` are their sources, for reference |

Not vendored: `vita2d_font.c` (FreeType), `vita2d_pgf.c`, `vita2d_pvf.c`,
`vita2d_image_png.c`, `vita2d_image_jpeg.c`, `vita2d_image_bmp.c`,
`texture_atlas.c`, `bin_packing_2d.c`, `int_htab.c`.  `vita2d.h` still
declares their functions; nothing here calls them.  Text is drawn by
`gpsp/vita/video_vita_text.c` (stb_truetype), images are decoded by
`psp/stb_image.h`.

## Local changes

1. `vita2d_get_back_fb()` added (and declared in `include/vita2d.h`): the
   display buffer being drawn, where upstream only exposes the front one.
   `vid_dump_ge()` reads the finished frame back from it before the swap.
2. With `-DVITA2D_NO_PGF` (which `ui.mk` passes) `vita2d_init` does not load
   the system PGF font module: no PGF font is used.
3. `vita2d_swap_state()` exposes pending/displayed state for the frontend pacer.
4. R7: three full-capacity temporary-pool banks are retired with independent
   vertex/fragment scene notifications. Checked/nonblocking scene admission,
   bounded pending-swap tracking and versioned fragment-reader fences let
   the backend skip a busy frame and callers defer texture publication
   without a new whole-GPU wait. Pool allocation failure, exact capacity,
   non-power-of-two alignment and arithmetic bounds are checked. The
   corresponding declarations live in `include/vita2d.h`.

5. `_vita2d_create_empty_texture_format_advanced` allocates the texture
   with `calloc`, not `malloc`: a plain texture never set `gxm_rtgt` or
   `depth_UID`, yet `vita2d_free_texture` reads both, so a reused heap chunk
   made it destroy a render target and free a GPU memory block it did not
   own (`gpu/native_geometry_test.c --texture-destructor`).

To take a newer upstream: retain these local changes and the R7 actual-native
delayed-consumption regression tests; upstream pool rotation alone is not a
completion/ownership guarantee. R7's hardware visual/performance validation
is separate from host model and native compile evidence.
